      "data": {
        "text": "Muybridge, The Horse in Motion (1878): the first motion study, run through a Scan Processor-style scan processor.\nThis patch needs a clip, and the Video Player starts empty. The demo clip is a separate download on the Video Research Unit release page (the demos zip, in its clip folder). It is also on Wikimedia Commons: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muybridge_race_horse_animated.gif (public domain; that file is a GIF, so convert it to MP4 first).\nAny video file works. Right-click the Video Player, choose Open video file..., then press PLAY. LOOP is already on.\nTry this: turn LUMA GAIN and INTENSITY on the Scan Processor, change Scanlines, or switch on ROTATE 90. Two slow LFOs already move LUMA GAIN (between 0.15 and 0.45) and INTENSITY (between 0.8 and 1.6), turned down by the 8vert so the horse stays in frame and lit."
      }
    }
  ],
